ems to be or that it comes  and goes and it seems to be to do with  population density and then for  thousands of years everything that you  get horrible things that set it back  like Emperor's and you know Wars and  basically predators you know there's  always a tendency of human beings to to  plunder each other and that can set the  whole process back what seems to have  happened around 1800  there are lots of different versions of  this I mean a lot of people say that for  that ideas started meeting each other  much better through the medium of  science and that kind of thing I don't  myself think that I think it's all about  fossil fuels ie that when we started  getting really cheap sources of energy  we could amplify the work we do and the  secret of modern society and the secret  of prosperity is that we're working for  each other each of us is working for  each other so a feature must amplifies  our work with a huge dose of fossil fuel  energy then we can do all the more for  each other so we can make each other  more prosperous and so I think that the  reason it takes off around 1800 and the  rate of growth of the world suddenly  gets a lot faster then and doesn't have  so many setbacks that there are some in  individual countries is because of  fossil fuels nice you're still an energy  determinist so well you've done your  best to dissuade me over the years and  maybe you'll succeed one day but not yet  but one of the ways when you say you're  working we work for each other you have  a wonderful analogy about the number of  people it took to prepare the Sun King  the king of Francis meals and you  compare that to what today how does that  work thank you yeah I think the king  louis xiv of france had 498 people to  prepare his dinner every night  it's allegedly that's what I've read but  you and I have 498 people to prepare our  lunch today by which I mean that within  10 miles of here there are at least 498  restaurants that you or I could go to  and each o