ere  we're at a time of financial crisis now  there's a climate change problem  possibly so what is it for you first  since you're going to look like well my  estimation and you know I'm no better  forecasting the future than anyone else  is that we will have some pretty dire  times as a result of the financial  crisis in the West and they could you  know they could last a long time I don't  know but that on the whole that won't  interrupt the improvement in average  living standards across the globe  because China and India is still  experiencing growth and there's evidence  that Africa is joining in increasingly  Latin America is doing better  etc so large proportion of the planet is  going to see this recession as a local  problem not as a global problem as for  the longer term there will be Wars there  will be drought there will be  earthquakes they'll be volcanoes  there'll be all sorts of horrible things  happened  the human race as it happened in the  20th century and the 20th century was a  pretty bad century from the point of  view of wars and dictatorships and  things like that and yet throughout that  period human living standards inexorably  rose and so that's what I think is going  to happen in the 21st century as for  climate well I think there is a small  problem small possibility of a big  disaster but there is a very large  probability of a moderate change in the  climate which will actually mostly be  beneficial  slightly warmer weather slightly more  moisture in the air will produce  slightly higher crop yields and  relatively little impact on things like  storms and droughts and species range  and so on now I might be wrong and we've  course got to prepare for the outside  possibilities of things being badly  wrong but I don't myself think it is  probable that we will face a bad century  but there is always the problem that you  have identified is that there are groups  of human beings will call them  chieftains priests and thieves I believe  you